/-!
# Structurality from `Equation153` through the companion `x □ y = (x ◇ ((y ◇ y) ◇ (x ◇ y)))`

Generated by `defwork/wffit.py`.  `Equation153` is `x = (x ◇ x) ◇ (y ◇ x)`.  The source half is
`AutBox.WordRigidFull`: two finite models of `Equation153` on one carrier with the same table of
`(x ◇ ((y ◇ y) ◇ (x ◇ y)))` are the same model.  That is what makes the companion's automorphisms automorphisms of
`◇`, and it mentions no map, so `grind` can do it.  Each theorem below then only has to check that
the source forces its target of the companion.
-/

open FirstOrder FirstOrder.Language Law Law.MagmaLaw FreeMagma

set_option maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option linter.unusedSimpArgs false
